# Adversarial read-only review — increments 001 + 002 (deepseek-flash)

**Mode:** read-only. **Ran:** `tests/test_cascade.py` + `tests/test_cascade_app.py` (18 passed), full suite once (`2504 passed in 378s`, G-011 did not fire), ~10 standalone probes.

**Tree note / premise correction.** The brief says the editor "is NOT yet cascaded — known, by design", but the working tree **does** contain increment 003 (`_on_task_edited` routes dates through `_apply_cascade`; `ProjectModal` has `#f-date-links`). I reviewed the cumulative diff as it exists; this affects DS-2 and the "editor between a bump and `m`" question. I verified both editor behaviours instead of trusting the note.

## Findings

### DS-1 — MEDIUM — `_short_title` crashes on an empty/blank title
`taskboard/app.py:1083-1091` (`out = words[0]`, line 1086). `split()` → `[]` raises `IndexError`. Titles are not guaranteed non-empty: `Task.from_dict` does `d.get("title","Untitled")` (`models.py:857`), so a board file / teammate push with `"title": ""` loads fine but the first cascade toast that names it raises. Move is applied+saved; toast is lost. **Fix:** `words = t.split(); if not words: return ""`. **Repro EXECUTED:** `_short_title("",12)` → `IndexError`; full path `action_due_bump → _apply_cascade → _cascade_toast → _short_title` traceback; via `pilot.press("+")` the exception is swallowed and no Toast appears while dates still move.

### DS-2 — MEDIUM — the toast formats `None` when the moved task has no due
`taskboard/app.py:1101` + `1145` (`_md(nd)`; `_md` = `f"{d:%b} {d.day}"`, `app.py:38`). A move with `due_delta == 0` on a task whose due is `None` leaves `moved[task] = (start, None)` → `TypeError`. Bump can't hit it (`dd=±1`), but the editor can: a task with a start and **no due**, editing only its **start** calls `_apply_cascade(task, sd, 0)` (`app.py:1878`). Engine is fine; only the toast dies. **Fix:** guard the lead when `nd is None`. **Repro EXECUTED:** Shim `_cascade_toast` on `start=today, due=None`, `plan_move(...,1,0)` → `TypeError`; undated-task bump control toasts fine.

### DS-3 — LOW — `together` counts an undated dependent as "moved"
`models.py:1936-1938` / `put` `models.py:1930-1934`; consumed at `app.py:1099-1100`,`1126-1141`. Under `together` every downstream task is put with `shift=due_delta` even with no dates → `plan.moved[id]=(None,None)`, counted/named by the toast. Contract clause is "WHO moved". TC-631 exercises this but only asserts `"moved" in said`. **Fix:** only put tasks whose planned dates differ (or filter `(None,None)` in the toast). **Repro EXECUTED:** toast `moved 5 +1d each` while `moved["u9"]==(None,None)` (only 4 moved).

### DS-4 — MEDIUM — AT-611 has no test node anywhere
`01-requirements.md:183,291`; `increment-001.md:9` ("AT-607..AT-611 arrive with 002/003"). 002/003 delivered 607-610; `grep -rn "AT-611\|AT_611" tests/` → nothing. §5 requires "one node each"; §5.2 "every HLR has a passing AT". Behaviours are covered at unit level (TC-619/620/621/622) and executed in `p1-thresholds.txt`, but the black-box AT is absent. **Fix:** add the AT-611 node or formally fold it and amend the contract.

### DS-5 — LOW — the tested `restore` is not the code path the app runs
`models.py:2018-2023`; app never imports it — `action_undo` inline loops `app.py:1280-1284`, `action_cascade_mode` `app.py:1202-1206`. TC-623/630 test `restore`, but production duplicates it → false confidence, drift risk. **Fix:** call `restore(...)`.

### DS-6 — LOW — unused import `bump_due`
`app.py:21`; after inc-003 nothing calls it (only the docstring at `app.py:1071`). Inc-002's reverse-census A3 ("increment 003 still uses it") is no longer true. **Fix:** drop the import.

### DS-7 — LOW — `CASCADE_VERB` has no `"push"` entry
`app.py:1081`. `plan_move` accepts `"push"`; `_apply_cascade(mode="push")` would `KeyError`. Unreachable today; a landmine. **Fix:** add `"push": "pushed"` or assert.

### Observations
- **`m` after `u`** (EXECUTED): entry is gone, `m` refuses verbatim, writes nothing — consistent with LLR-604.4/§6.3.
- **Editor between bump and `m`** (EXECUTED): title-only save pushes no undo entry → `m` re-applies correctly; date-changing save pushes its own entry → `m` re-applies that.
- **`save_atomic` failure mid-cascade** (`app.py:1172-1183`): memory ahead of disk with the undo entry already pushed; inherited single-task posture.
- **`m` clobbers intervening non-undoable changes** (e.g. team sync) by restoring snapshot dates; same as shipped undo.

